    "updated_at": "2022-01-20T03:54:02Z",
    "body": "According to [the spec][1], devices are protected \"if and only if\" their `bInterfaceClass` is equal to one of the following values:\r\n\r\nCode | Description\r\n-- | --\r\n0x01 | Audio\r\n0x03 | HID (Human Interface Device)\r\n0x08 | Mass Storage\r\n0x0B | Smart Card\r\n0x0E | Video\r\n0x10 | Audio/Video Devices\r\n0xE0 | Wireless Controller\r\n\r\nYou can use the **Devices** tab at `chrome://usb-internals` to quickly render all of the descriptors for a device.\r\n\r\nMass storage devices are generally protected. There's [a rational in the spec][2] too.\r\n\r\n[1]: https://wicg.github.io/webusb/#protected-interface-classes\r\n[2]: https://wicg.github.io/webusb/#security-and-privacy",
